WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.080
<i>Please.</i>

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.320
<i>Please let the new form of IDOLiSH7...</i>

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.870
It's time for our next guest!

00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:22.370
<i>...be accepted by everyone.</i>

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:38.890
Their center has changed from
 Nanase Riku-kun to Izumi Iori-kun!

00:00:41.010 --> 00:00:42.460
They'll be singing...

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:51.020
Do you want to hear me sing?

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:54.950
Then I'll sing to thank you 
for that delicious cake.

00:00:56.290 --> 00:00:58.240
Sing with me.

00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:01.680
Let's sing my song—Zero's song together.

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:06.590
Then he sang for me!

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:10.130
And that's how the legendary 
idol Zero and I met.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:14.010
Lucky! I've only ever seen him on TV.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.160
I've only ever heard his name.

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.500
Is he really that cool?

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.640
People say he's the origin 
of the current idol boom.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:25.880
He was only active for three years,

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:30.920
but it's said his economic impact exceeded
 100 billion yen by the time he disappeared.

00:01:31.620 --> 00:01:33.160
Wow.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:37.980
If he was so popular, why'd he disappear?

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:44.860
Didn't Zero's songwriter, Sakura Haruki-san,
travel to your country to look for him?

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:46.280
Yes!

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:51.780
Back then, Haruki entrusted me 
with the songs he wrote for Zero.

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:55.220
Did he say what kind of 
person Zero was like?

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:57.860
Zero's songs are magic.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:02.520
He said he was like a wizard of happiness.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.230
A wizard, huh?

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:06.920
Speaking of Zero,

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:10.190
apparently Zero Arena is 
going to be remodeled soon.

00:02:10.190 --> 00:02:13.530
They'll likely hold a grand 
inauguration for it.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:17.740
Inauguration? Is that like an infestation?

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:23.160
It's the very first performance 
held at a new theater.

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.390
It's an opportunity to seize 
the world's attention,

00:02:25.390 --> 00:02:28.120
so they'll invite major players 
to their first performance.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.460
Huh...

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:35.440
They'll probably invite top stars to rival 
Zero for their first performance.

00:02:37.620 --> 00:02:39.380
I'm back.

00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:42.370
Welcome back, Manager. Wait...

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:43.860
You're crying?!

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:45.420
What happened?!

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:49.600
I have some very important news for you.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:50.700
News?

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:57.950
I've worked with you as the manager 
of IDOLiSH7 until now, but I...

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:00.640
<i>This preface...</i>

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:03.070
<i>Is it because my lectures were too long?</i>

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.450
<i>Because I practiced my choreography 
at a filming for a drama?</i>

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:09.260
<i>Because I got along too well 
with major band members</i>

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:11.240
<i>and went drinking with 
them after a recording?</i>

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:14.160
<i>Because I ate King Pudding during class?</i>

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:16.760
<i>Because I tried too hard to manage 
MEZZO"'s schedule on my own</i>

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:19.130
<i>after she said I could talk 
to her about anything?</i>

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:23.180
<i>Because I caused a commotion taking 
commemorative photos with my lady fans?!</i>

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:27.860
<i>Because I stayed up late practicing my dancing 
after she told me not to push myself too hard?</i>

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:30.770
A-Are you quitting—

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:31.740
Finally!

00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:36.020
I got you a job that will 
let me return the favor!

00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:37.770
What?

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:42.020
There's going to be an IDOLiSH7 
regular namesake show!

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:42.030
"IDOLiSH7 Regular Namesake Show (Temp)"

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:46.250
You did it, guys.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.760
You finally got a namesake show.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:50.160
Congratulations.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:53.210
You and the manager worked 
really hard for this.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:55.840
Boss.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:56.830
Banri-san.

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:59.970
This is the theme song for your show.

00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:02.840
I'd decided a while ago 
that this might be nice.

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:06.670
Our theme song...

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.830
Excuse me, Manager.

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:13.240
What about sponsors?

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:15.080
Don't worry.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:20.190
It will be focused around IT companies with 
few ties to business and political circles.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:21.750
That's good.

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.990
It's because of your hard work.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:27.570
Both MEZZO" and our names 
have spread far enough

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.060
that your dad can't interfere.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:34.620
Your show was also confirmed 
thanks to Mitsuki-kun's

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:36.890
hard work on <i>The TV Man Show</i>.

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:38.620
Oh, great!

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:39.140
Who, me?

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:43.880
Remember how Mr. Shimooka-san was absent 
at the end of the year because of the flu?

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.810
Everyone loved how you stepped in.

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:49.000
You're right.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:51.390
You saved us then.

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.570
You changed the subject and 
kept the conversation going.

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:55.570
It's what you always do.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:58.580
You do the same thing during 
MC breaks at our concerts.

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.890
You keep everything together 
so we don't go off-topic.

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:05.440
Well, it's not like I did anything special...

00:05:05.440 --> 00:05:10.710
What's normal to you is a valuable 
talent in the television world.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:17.050
Mr. Shimooka-san had a lot of 
nice things to say about you.

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.650
Thank you, Mitsuki-kun.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:23.020
Thanks to your talent, 
we got a namesake show.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:26.180
Because of me?

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:28.770
Your work has been recognized.

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:30.780
Impressive, Mitsuki-san!

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:33.420
Mikki, I'm super glad you're part of the group.

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:37.230
I love it when you talk, Mitsuki!

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:40.810
Your voice and the way you speak 
give me energy and smiles!

00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.480
Thanks, Mitsuki!

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:49.100
Don't flatter me.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:53.190
I'm going to the bathroom.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.160
I thought he'd be overjoyed.

00:05:58.160 --> 00:05:59.750
That was a subdued reaction.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:02.740
Nah, he's definitely gonna 
go cry in the bathroom.

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:11.560
Yes! Yes!

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:12.480
See?

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:18.520
Nii-san's long-cherished desire 
has finally been realized.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:22.160
The world has finally recognized his talent.

00:06:22.490 --> 00:06:24.250
The same goes for you boys.

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:27.850
Your uniqueness has incredible value.

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:29.980
You've been recognized by professionals.

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:36.290
That's why you've been given a show 
with a huge budget and staff.

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:40.320
Thank you so much for working so hard.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:41.840
Yes!

00:06:49.330 --> 00:06:52.170
I'd like to go to the bathroom soon...

00:06:52.170 --> 00:06:53.660
Try to hold it.

00:06:53.660 --> 00:06:54.850
What?

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:58.100
This is our moment of truth!

00:06:58.100 --> 00:06:59.850
Let's give everything we've got!

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:04.290
I'll study how people MC 
and talk on other shows.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.110
You're really excited, Mitsu.

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:08.980
I mean, I finally get to be useful.

00:07:09.380 --> 00:07:12.990
I'm not good at singing, I'm a bad dancer,

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:15.900
I'm short, and I don't have 
any talent for acting...

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:20.670
I met Zero, came to admire him,
and ultimately made it this far

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:23.310
because of you guys.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:25.010
What are you talking about?

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:28.970
If you weren't here, we couldn't 
have made it this far.

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:31.810
That's right, Nii-san.

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:34.800
It's fine. It's just how I feel.

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:41.390
Finally... Finally, I have a chance to 
repay you guys for making me an idol.

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.430
How could I not be excited?

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:44.940
Mitsuki...

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:48.380
The name of the show will 
be <i>Lovely Night With You!</i>

00:07:48.380 --> 00:07:53.180
You'll be taking on challenges 
along with your audience.

00:07:53.850 --> 00:07:54.820
Sounds interesting.

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:57.170
To advertise the show,

00:07:57.170 --> 00:08:01.790
you'll be appearing in more promos as guests 
on other programs produced by the station.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:03.630
Promos, huh?

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:04.970
We're really doing this.

00:08:04.970 --> 00:08:07.700
You have a lot of guest appearances 
during prime time, too.

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:09.970
You've also been invited 
onto Re:vale's show.

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:11.420
<i>The</i> Re:vale?!

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:16.800
Yes. Re:vale, the overall champions 
of the <i>Black or White</i>.

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:18.510
I admire them.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:21.220
Momo-san and Yuki-san are both so cool!

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:22.510
I'm a fan, myself.

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:24.390
What? Really?

00:08:24.390 --> 00:08:26.740
I have all of their CDs.

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:30.650
I look to them for ideas on how to 
handle public relations for IDOLiSH7.

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:33.910
It's amazing that we're appearing 
on Re:vale's show...

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:37.490
We've appeared with them on big shows before,

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:40.290
but we only ever got to 
exchange basic introductions.

00:08:40.850 --> 00:08:42.520
Re:vale, huh?

00:08:42.520 --> 00:08:44.060
What is it?

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:45.540
Oh, it's nothing...

00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:47.820
On top of your existing work,

00:08:47.820 --> 00:08:52.620
you'll probably be busy recording for 
your show and appearing in promos.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:55.060
I'm happier that way.

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:56.340
I'll do my best.

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:58.050
Let's do our best!

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:59.310
Yes!

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.270
<b>Namesake Show</b>

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.270
<b>Lovely Night with You!</b>

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.270
<b>Newfound Fame! 
Double-sided IDOLiSH7
 Poster Included!</b>

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:07.270
<b>Lovely Night With You!
I7 supporting various viewer challenges</b>

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:27.230
Today's guest is IDOLiSH7!

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:28.790
Thanks for having us.

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:30.790
<b>I Love Tamaki-kun</b>

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:30.790
<b>IDOLiSH7 Tamaki LOVE</b>

00:09:30.790 --> 00:09:32.730
Listen to them cheer.

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:33.950
Well, you are handsome.

00:09:33.950 --> 00:09:36.010
Keep it down. I can hear you.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:38.300
<b>First Appearance!</b>

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:38.300
<b>Let's Find Out Why They're So Popular!</b>

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:38.310
Tamaki-san is incredibly popular.

00:09:37.070 --> 00:09:39.130
<i>I said keep it down!</i>

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:42.560
MEZZO" was always popular, 
but since the new year

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:46.150
he's made more variety show 
appearances, rising above the rest.

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:50.690
Do you know why Yotsuba-san is so popular?

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:53.570
His appearance or dancing...

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:56.570
I know it's not what he wants,

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:59.570
<b>IDOLiSH7's Izumi Mitsuki: "I'm Considerate
 and Support My Friends From the Shadows"</b>

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:59.570
<b>Strength Behind the Scenes</b>

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:59.570
The Idol Who Never Smiles

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:59.570
<b>Yotsuba Tamaki IDOLiSH7 Special!</b>

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:59.570
<b>The Truth About His Younger Sister...</b>

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:59.580
but people are talking 
about his sister as well.

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:04.580
<b>Popular Idols</b>

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:04.580
<b>Seven Men Overflowing With Personality</b>

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:04.580
But I think the biggest reason is that 
Tamaki-san is close to his audience.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:05.830
That's right.

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:08.980
He acts bored when he's bored

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:12.840
and boldly vocalizes the 
thoughts viewers want to say.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:17.080
In that way, Yotsuba-san is 
the opposite of my brother.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:17.090
<b>IDOLiSH7's Izumi Mitsuki: "I'm Considerate
 and Support My Friends From the Shadows"</b>

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:17.090
<b>Strength Behind the Scenes</b>

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:17.090
<b>The Idol Who Never Smiles</b>

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:17.090
<b>Yotsuba Tamaki IDOLiSH7 Special!</b>

00:10:17.080 --> 00:10:21.090
My brother is close to creators, and 
Yotsuba-san is close to the audience.

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:26.480
<b>Popular Idols</b>

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:26.480
<b>Seven Men Overflowing With Personality</b>

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:26.470
My brother's co-stars like him because he does
 his best to make boring talk shows exciting.

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:33.410
But sometimes that laughter can 
feel forced to an audience.

00:10:33.980 --> 00:10:37.120
The creators and the audience...

00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:38.740
Put another way,

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:42.790
with these two in our group, 
we have nothing to fear.

00:10:43.860 --> 00:10:50.950
We also have the powerful singer and 
lovable genius, Nanase-san.

00:10:52.130 --> 00:10:54.660
Iori, you're still not leaving?

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:55.630
Manager?

00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:57.640
Good evening, Riku-san.

00:10:58.070 --> 00:11:00.670
You guys were talking alone again?

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:03.740
Nanase-san, you can leave without me.

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:05.860
You're going to <i>keep</i> talking alone?

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:09.380
Yes. Now stop interrupting and leave.

00:11:09.380 --> 00:11:10.440
Hey, wait!

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:12.740
Let's resume our conversation.

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:15.440
Nanase-san is a genius 
overflowing with charm.

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:20.390
What we need in this age are lovable 
and charming stars like Zero.

00:11:20.390 --> 00:11:22.620
If we focus on promoting 
the group around Nanase-san—

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:24.210
Hey, listen.

00:11:24.210 --> 00:11:28.620
Don't you think it's weird that you guys 
spend so much time alone together?

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.200
I told you not to interrupt!

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:31.220
Hey, wait—

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:33.640
See? You always need to be on your guard.

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:36.160
You should go home, warm up, and rest.

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:38.500
Got it?

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:44.720
The person you just kicked out of the room 
is that genius overflowing with charm, right?

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.770
Onstage he is.

00:11:46.770 --> 00:11:51.270
Aside from that, he's a naive and 
spoiled boy with a brother complex.

00:11:51.270 --> 00:11:52.970
B-But...

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:54.970
Let me make a prediction.

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:59.650
Once our namesake show begins airing, 
we'll receive offers from other places.

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:03.330
Our time is right there, waiting for us.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:08.480
And tomorrow is Re:vale's show.

00:12:06.030 --> 00:12:10.040
Re:vale Dressing Room

00:12:10.670 --> 00:12:13.850
D-Do you think they're scary people?

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:15.410
When I looked online,

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:19.450
I kept getting results like "Re:vale 
rage" and "Re:vale bad blood."

00:12:19.450 --> 00:12:20.950
What?

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:22.390
They're not scary.

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:24.870
There's nothing scary about them.

00:12:24.870 --> 00:12:26.740
Come on, relax.

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:29.900
Could you not make it sound like 
you're trying to hypnotize me?

00:12:30.290 --> 00:12:34.540
I'm sure you all know already, 
but let's go over it again.

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:35.440
Manager.

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:36.690
Y-Yes!

00:12:37.030 --> 00:12:41.280
Re:vale's Momo-san is 
cheerful and popular.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.520
He's currently very active on variety shows.

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:47.500
The shows Momo-san appears on 
are always cheerful and fun.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:49.980
He must be a kind person, then.

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:52.420
Are you aware that your 
hyper-acrimonious twin brother

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:56.040
is known as "a modern day angel" on TV?

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.750
Tenn-nii <i>is</i> an angel!

00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:58.910
Damn your brother complex...

00:12:59.910 --> 00:13:01.420
Next, there's Yuki-san.

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:04.010
He has a cool and calm feel.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:07.050
He's received high praise for his acting.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:09.070
Yuki-san is cool.

00:13:09.070 --> 00:13:10.900
I cried when I saw the movie he starred in.

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:13.830
Remember that historical drama 
he was in with Chiba Shizuo-san?

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:15.950
I saw that, too!

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:18.140
Wabi-sabi, harakiri!

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:19.990
It was fantastic!

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:21.580
Yamato-san, did you see it?

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:22.230
No.

00:13:22.230 --> 00:13:23.150
Oh?

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:24.830
They're the great Re:vale.

00:13:24.830 --> 00:13:28.490
They might be fussy when 
it comes to etiquette.

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:31.310
I-I'll be careful.

00:13:31.310 --> 00:13:34.380
Now let's get ready to 
rumble and go greet them!

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:35.640
Yes!

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:37.670
You make it sound like 
we're conducting a raid...

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:40.410
Excuse us.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:53.930
This is Takanashi Productions' IDOLiSH7, 
and I'm their manager, Takanashi.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:56.260
Thank you for having us today.

00:13:56.260 --> 00:13:58.760
Thank you!

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:00.620
Huh.

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:02.270
IDOLiSH7?

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:06.480
<i>This isn't good. They seem unhappy.</i>

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:09.200
<i>Were the theories about 
them being scary real?</i>

00:14:10.610 --> 00:14:11.970
Uh, um—

00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:14.610
Oh, you're the group that beat TRIGGER.

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:16.530
You there, can I tell you something?

00:14:16.530 --> 00:14:18.210
Wh-Who, me?

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:21.090
Wait. If you have any 
questions, I'll answer them.

00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:22.920
You'll do, then.

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:24.420
What is it?

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:27.740
At <i>Black or White</i>...

00:14:28.660 --> 00:14:30.680
You guys were really great!

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:32.180
What?

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:34.290
I was so moved!

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:37.130
Your singing and dancing were both great!

00:14:37.130 --> 00:14:39.570
I've been so excited to meet you!

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:43.110
But since you guys were 
talking about us being scary,

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:45.550
you tickled the mischievous imp inside me.

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:48.350
I tried being as scary as possible.

00:14:48.350 --> 00:14:50.070
Well? Were you surprised?

00:14:50.070 --> 00:14:51.980
Oh, uh...

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:56.630
Come on, Momo. If you talk so much 
at once, you'll startle them.

00:14:56.630 --> 00:14:59.830
Yeah, but there's <i>so much</i> I wanna say!

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:02.480
Sorry for scaring you.

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:06.100
I'm Yuki of Re:vale.

00:15:06.100 --> 00:15:07.710
Thanks for coming today.

00:15:07.710 --> 00:15:11.220
We don't bite, so feel free to relax.

00:15:11.220 --> 00:15:13.730
That's right, pretend you're at Yuki's house.

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:15.000
My house?

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:19.140
He's got a huge sofa, but 
the cushions are so tiny.

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:20.780
They fit in your hand.

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:21.930
I can only fit my ear on them.

00:15:21.930 --> 00:15:23.240
You don't do that!

00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:25.550
It's surprisingly relaxing.

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:27.550
You're hopeless, Momo.

00:15:26.750 --> 00:15:29.860
They seem like really nice people.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:33.340
No wonder they're Japan's top stars.

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:35.400
Momo... Yuki...

00:15:36.610 --> 00:15:38.420
They're Momorin and Yukirin!

00:15:38.420 --> 00:15:39.330
Tamaki-kun!

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:44.430
It's fine. Momorin makes 
me just like this juice.

00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:46.870
Peach and apple sparkling...

00:15:46.870 --> 00:15:48.290
Or "peach-apple" (momo-rin) for short.

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:50.040
I drink it all the time.

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:51.470
You guys can have some!

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:53.770
Thank you.

00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:55.460
Thanks for having us today.

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:57.350
Sure. Glad to have you.

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:02.430
Excuse me.

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:05.240
Could we try that one more time?

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:07.630
I know this is rehearsal,
but this is your fifth take.

00:16:07.630 --> 00:16:09.520
Re:vale's waiting, you know.

00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:10.940
Sorry.

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:14.900
If you put so much pressure on 
him, it'll be harder to sing.

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:18.340
Yeah. We're good.

00:16:18.340 --> 00:16:21.380
If you're tired, why don't we take a break?

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:23.470
Wouldn't that be trouble for—

00:16:23.470 --> 00:16:27.850
You can't act like a big man unless 
you take care of your juniors.

00:16:27.850 --> 00:16:29.620
Could we take a break?

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:32.030
Chan-Momo, you're too soft.

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:35.270
Sorry, sorry. I'll make it up to you.

00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:37.380
Let's take a break!

00:16:38.210 --> 00:16:39.500
Hey, you.

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:41.130
Me?

00:16:41.360 --> 00:16:44.020
Can't you smile more during 
the talking parts?

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:46.280
Smiling is part of your job.

00:16:48.870 --> 00:16:50.010
Sorry.

00:16:50.010 --> 00:16:52.210
Don't worry about us.

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:54.990
Once you have juniors, you can help them.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:58.280
Yeah, just sing like you always do.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:16:59.430
I expect great things from you.

00:16:59.800 --> 00:17:02.310
Momo, don't put pressure on him.

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:06.040
Whoa! Sorry, I didn't mean to. Just relax.

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:07.280
Should I make funny faces?

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:11.870
I'm fine. Thank you.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:14.220
Mitsuki!

00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:16.560
Mitsuki, come here a sec!

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:18.380
Okay.

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:22.680
You know this segment?

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:27.280
The script has me running it, 
but you should try MCing.

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:29.020
What?! On the spot?

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:30.660
You came to promote your show.

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:32.950
You should show off how
interesting you guys are.

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:34.440
Ah, b-but...

00:17:34.910 --> 00:17:37.140
You worked hard for your 
namesake show, right?

00:17:37.140 --> 00:17:41.820
Other places are waiting to see 
what you'll do because of the FSC,

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:44.450
but if it goes well,
you'll get tons more work.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:47.960
The FSC? You know about that?

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:51.970
Don't underestimate my information network.

00:17:51.970 --> 00:17:54.900
I even know what color underwear 
the queen of commercials wears.

00:17:54.900 --> 00:17:55.720
Her under—

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:57.680
I'm joking. Did you imagine it?

00:17:57.680 --> 00:17:59.100
N-No way!

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:03.670
Don't worry. Shimooka-chan 
told us all about you.

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:05.580
I'll vouch for you, too.

00:18:05.580 --> 00:18:07.300
But, if I mess up...

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:09.800
Just laugh if you do!

00:18:09.800 --> 00:18:14.210
Crying or screaming about it won't change 
anything, so it's better to laugh!

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:17.410
After all, we're cute idols.

00:18:20.110 --> 00:18:21.540
It's true.

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:25.720
This boy never smiles.

00:18:25.720 --> 00:18:28.090
What's your problem? Don't touch my face.

00:18:28.360 --> 00:18:31.840
I think it's fine. I didn't smile, either.

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:36.920
If you smile when you're bored, people 
will stop making interesting things.

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:40.000
I said, don't touch my face!

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:44.980
Instead, you have to make things 
interesting when they're boring.

00:18:45.590 --> 00:18:46.470
Me?

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:48.790
Do you like being bored?

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:49.610
I hate it.

00:18:49.610 --> 00:18:52.750
Entertain yourself, then.

00:18:52.750 --> 00:18:55.700
This is our space. You can do anything.

00:18:55.700 --> 00:18:58.460
I can do what's fun for me?

00:18:58.460 --> 00:18:59.750
Of course.

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:04.430
When we're having fun, our fun reaches 
the other side of the camera.

00:19:04.430 --> 00:19:08.460
But I was told to do a proper job.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:13.180
There's a difference between being 
impolite and being a passive guest.

00:19:13.870 --> 00:19:16.860
If we wanted a polite boy,
 we wouldn't have invited you.

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:21.070
Make them shudder. Excite them.

00:19:21.070 --> 00:19:24.430
I want to see the exceptionally 
cool Yotsuba Tamaki.

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:31.220
Try entertaining us, and your sister who's 
watching from the other side of the TV.

00:19:31.670 --> 00:19:34.180
We're ready to start!

00:19:34.180 --> 00:19:36.500
Okay. Riku, are you okay?

00:19:36.500 --> 00:19:37.930
Yes, I'm fine!

00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:42.150
Okay. Then let's have some 
fun together tonight.

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:44.650
Sorry if we keep you up all night.

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:48.280
Let's work and be happy together!

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:49.950
Thank you for working with us!

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:52.310
Thank you!

00:19:49.960 --> 00:19:52.440
<b>Recording In Progress</b>

00:19:52.440 --> 00:19:53.460
<b>Recording In Progress</b>

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:57.880
Today's guest is IDOLiSH7!

00:19:57.880 --> 00:19:58.740
Yay!

00:19:58.740 --> 00:19:59.750
Yeah!

00:19:58.910 --> 00:20:00.200
Thanks for having us!

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:05.720
Winners of the JIMA New Artist Award and 
the <i>Black or White</i> Men's Idol Award.

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:08.690
Some amazing new artists 
have shown up, Yuki.

00:20:08.690 --> 00:20:11.070
The nail that sticks out must 
be hammered down quickly.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:14.440
Please, go easy on us.

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:17.030
We're frozen solid with anxiety.

00:20:17.030 --> 00:20:18.110
Right, Riku?

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:19.600
Yeah...

00:20:20.430 --> 00:20:22.000
He really is nervous.

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:23.900
Sorry, Riku.

00:20:23.900 --> 00:20:27.960
It's Yuki's fault for teasing you when 
you came to see us in our dressing room.

00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:30.770
N-N-No one teased me!

00:20:30.770 --> 00:20:32.940
Could you not make it seem 
like I actually did?

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:36.170
<b>Due to noise concerns, please use the other 
door while recording is in progress. 
Echoing may occur.</b>

00:20:36.490 --> 00:20:39.170
They were amazing.

00:20:39.170 --> 00:20:40.630
Yeah.

00:20:40.630 --> 00:20:42.670
It's not just that.

00:20:43.750 --> 00:20:45.970
It was kind of fun.

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:47.960
We're ready to start!

00:20:47.960 --> 00:20:49.680
Okay!

00:20:51.910 --> 00:20:53.430
It's starting.

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:27.230
You understood me even without words

00:21:27.230 --> 00:21:33.850
I never doubted why

00:21:33.850 --> 00:21:39.990
Behind your smile there 
was a sense of uneasiness

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:45.910
Time passed without me realizing it

00:21:45.910 --> 00:21:52.250
I'll never say we should surrender

00:21:52.250 --> 00:21:59.270
If this is the TRUTH we've 
found, we can't stop

00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:02.430
Hold on to hope

00:22:02.430 --> 00:22:04.250
Sound on SILVER SKY

00:22:04.250 --> 00:22:09.380
Dancing in a sky that's about to rain

00:22:09.380 --> 00:22:15.470
I want to become the wind and blow on

00:22:15.470 --> 00:22:17.260
And then SILVER SKY

00:22:17.260 --> 00:22:22.430
The reason its ambiguous color changes

00:22:22.430 --> 00:22:32.660
Is because all we have is 
our love for each other

00:22:50.050 --> 00:22:52.570
<b>Recording In Progress</b>

00:22:52.570 --> 00:22:53.560
<b>Recording In Progress</b>

00:22:53.770 --> 00:22:55.550
Thank you!

00:22:55.800 --> 00:22:58.510
Thanks. You guys were great!

00:22:58.510 --> 00:23:01.550
The show was great because of you.

00:23:01.550 --> 00:23:05.810
I don't know how to thank you for 
all your kindness and generosity.

00:23:05.810 --> 00:23:09.530
Hey, have you heard about 
the Zero Arena inaugural show?

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:12.610
Yes, but nothing specific.

00:23:13.540 --> 00:23:16.350
The show's gonna take 
place over three days.

00:23:16.350 --> 00:23:19.390
The first day is TRIGGER, and 
we perform on the last day.

00:23:19.390 --> 00:23:22.330
They haven't chosen the 
second day's group yet.

00:23:22.620 --> 00:23:24.870
Wouldn't you like to take this spot?

00:23:24.870 --> 00:23:27.140
Us? We'd love to!

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:30.380
Spin in a circle and bark for me, then.

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:33.230
Woof!

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:33.790
<b>No Hesitation</b>

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:38.730
<b>Huh?!</b>

00:23:33.230 --> 00:23:33.670
What?

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:34.990
I was joking.

00:23:35.590 --> 00:23:38.730
Hey! Please don't make our 
center bark for no reason!

00:23:39.440 --> 00:23:41.220
How much of that was a joke?

00:23:41.220 --> 00:23:42.680
Were you joking about the show, too?

00:23:42.680 --> 00:23:44.940
That part's true!

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:48.430
But it's the manager of Zero 
Arena who makes the call.

00:23:48.430 --> 00:23:51.580
We'll recommend IDOLiSH7.

00:23:51.580 --> 00:23:55.840
Seize the opportunity and climb up here.

00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:00.080
A New Door
